## Claim-to-evidence coverage summary

Of the draft's 24 footnotes: **17 trace cleanly** to ledger clusters at medium-high confidence or better ([^2]–[^7], [^10]–[^12], [^14]–[^16], [^18]–[^19], [^21]–[^24]). **Five are compromised**: [^1] (square-footage attribution, F-13), [^8] (non-reproducible arithmetic, F-6/7/8/9), [^9] (wrong AAR author plus narrative excess, F-3/4), [^13] (contradicted flight count plus unsupported causal hinge, F-1/2), [^17] (self-referential, corroboration overstated, F-10). One in-text claim carries no footnote at all and needs one: the Virginia/DC code-adoption bridge (F-5). No footnote is fabricated; the pattern is drift and embellishment at the edges of real evidence, not invention of sources.

## The five most load-bearing claims, and whether each survives

1. **NFPA 72 / ACRP 175 / IEC 60268-16 define a testable intelligibility floor.** SURVIVES. Ten-plus corroborating records, primary regulation and TRB research (E-0073/74 cluster, E-0019 cluster, E-0042/52). The single best-supported proposition in the file. The *bridge* making it binding on MWAA (F-5) needs a source.
2. **The Design Manual is the enforceable vehicle ("force of law").** SURVIVES, with two caveats: the six-agent "corroboration" is six quotations of the same MWAA self-description, not independent verification; and what the manual already contains is unproven (F-12).
3. **The federal accessibility floor (49 CFR 27.71, 14 CFR 382.53, ADAAG) mandates redundant channels.** SURVIVES. Direct eCFR sourcing (E-0132/E-0133). Note 27.71 rests on a single agent's find — flag for fact-check priority, since so much of the argument stands on it.
4. **The cost is trivial relative to the program ($12M–$40M; $0.03–$0.11/enplanement).** DOES NOT SURVIVE AS STATED. The direction is safe; the figures are not reproducible and the denominators are mixed (F-6, F-7, F-8, F-9). This is the draft's largest repair job.
5. **The adoption window is now (before C/D and DCA T1 scopes harden).** SURVIVES FOR C/D ONLY. The C/D urgency is real and evidenced; DCA T1 imminence and the "scopes not yet advertised" window are asserted, not shown (F-11, F-15c).

